    {
      "id": "2",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 2,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p>Similarly to <span data-gp-id='1'>だ</span>, <span data-gp-id='2'>です</span> is an <span data-term='助動詞・じょどうし'>auxiliary verb</span> that is an expression of determination or assertion. It states that something 'is' a certain way. <span data-gp-id='2'>です</span> is considered to be the polite variation of <span data-gp-id='1'>だ</span>. Keep in mind though that although their roles are similar, both <span data-gp-id='1'>だ</span> and <span data-gp-id='2'>です</span> are standalone structures.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='2'>です</span> connects to words in exactly the same way as <span data-gp-id='1'>だ</span>, but is also regularly seen attached to the end of <span data-gp-id='24'>い-Adjectives</span>.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154683'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154684'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154685'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154686'>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='caution'><h4>Caution</h4>\r\n<p>Although <span data-gp-id='2'>です</span> is regularly attached to the end of <span data-gp-id='24'>い-Adjectives</span>, some may actually consider this incorrect Japanese, and it should not be used in formal writing. In daily spoken language/texting, however, it is completely normal.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n\r\n<li data-study-question='183747'>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The above example technically should not be used in formal writing. Despite this, in recent years, it is starting to become the norm.</p></section>"
      }
    },
